In .NET 10, MAUI adopts **edge-to-edge** rendering on Android by default, which means `adjustResize` alone no longer shrinks your layout when the keyboard appears. You need to react to **window insets** (specifically the IME inset).

## Recommended fix

In your **Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs**, apply bottom padding from the keyboard inset:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Android.OS.Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        var rootView = Window!.DecorView.FindViewById(Android.Resource.Id.Content)!;

        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(rootView, new InsetsListener());
    }

    private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var navBar = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

            // Use the larger of keyboard or nav bar bottom inset
            int bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navBar.Bottom);
            v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottom);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

Also ensure your **AndroidManifest.xml** still has:

```xml
<activity android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize" ... />
```

## Why this works

- **Edge-to-edge** means your app draws behind system bars and the keyboard area.
- `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` reports the keyboard height.
- Setting bottom padding on the root view pushes your content (including the input bar) above the keyboard.

## Alternative: disable edge-to-edge (quick workaround)

If you want the old .NET 9 behavior back temporarily:

```csharp
// In MainActivity.OnCreate, after base call:
AndroidX.Activity.EdgeToEdge.Disable(this);
```

This reverts to the legacy resize behavior but you'll lose the modern edge-to-edge look.
